Subject: [PATCH] serial: esp32_uart: allow five ports for the ESP32-P4

UART_NR is 3 in the driver, so aliases serial0..serial2 fit. The P4 has
five UART cores and the M5Stack Tab5 uses alias serial3 (Grove, UART2 at
500cc000) on top of serial0 (the console) and serial2 (RS485, UART1 at
500cb000): the Grove port failed its probe on every batch1 boot with

  esp32-uart 500cc000.serial: driver limited to 3 serial ports
  esp32-uart 500cc000.serial: probe with driver esp32-uart failed with error -12

and /dev/ttyS3 never appeared. Allow five; ESP32 and ESP32-S3 boards
carry no alias that high, so their behaviour does not change.

---
 drivers/tty/serial/esp32_uart.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/esp32_uart.c b/drivers/tty/serial/esp32_uart.c
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/esp32_uart.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/esp32_uart.c
@@ -18,7 +18,13 @@
 
 #define DRIVER_NAME	"esp32-uart"
 #define DEV_NAME	"ttyS"
-#define UART_NR		3
+/*
+ * The ESP32-P4 has five UART cores (UART0..4); the M5Stack Tab5 uses
+ * alias serial3 for its Grove port next to serial0 (console) and
+ * serial2 (RS485). Boards with fewer UARTs carry no alias that high,
+ * so a larger array changes nothing for them.
+ */
+#define UART_NR		5
 
 #define ESP32_UART_TX_FIFO_SIZE	127
 #define ESP32_UART_RX_FIFO_SIZE	127
